WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.385
Endpoint Detection and Response is a security capability that monitors endpoint activity,

00:00:05.385 --> 00:00:07.795
detects suspicious behavior, supports investigation,

00:00:07.795 --> 00:00:10.680
and helps responders contain or remediate threats.

00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:13.840
The detection part helps teams notice unusual or risky activity.

00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:17.200
The response part helps teams act before an incident spreads further.

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:21.465
EDR tools typically collect telemetry from endpoints, such as process execution,

00:00:21.465 --> 00:00:25.990
file activity, network connections, registry changes, login activity, script execution,

00:00:25.990 --> 00:00:27.950
and suspicious command-line behavior.

00:00:27.950 --> 00:00:31.840
This telemetry gives analysts a more detailed view than a simple allowed or blocked

00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:32.320
message.

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:34.305
The goal is not only to block known malware.

00:00:34.305 --> 00:00:37.720
The goal is to help security teams understand what happened, how far it spread,

00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:39.560
and what action should be taken next.

00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:44.160
EDR is especially useful when an event is not obviously good or bad and the analyst needs

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:44.680
context.
